{"name": "n1102-01", "sha256": "2f99c9d788165c3b25de4779d1da0764076a6cbde0097fffeb60ed8737951f4a", "words": 733, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.6310966610908508, "fraction_ai_assisted": 4.45246379324383e-23, "fraction_human": 0.36890333890914917, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/ddc8fda6-114b-42bc-85b6-7a82d9d0d8ab", "utc": "2026-11-02T18:53:56Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 228, 0, 1403, "Introduction\nWhen people tell me they have trauma, I generally recommend they follow my inner child therapy guide, which includes somatic therapy & breathwork. To help people engage more deeply with the practices, I have advised the use of my Ultimate Psychedelic protocol. But recently, I realized that there’s some more basic physiological interventions we need to implement before getting to those levels. The very first step is fixing your physical health and neuro-inflammation. I suggest starting with my detox guide. After addressing overall health and neuro-inflammation, this de-armoring guide gets more specific to address the hardened neural pathways that have developed over a lifetime.\nThis protocol is partly theoretical and partly based on experience reports. There’s no peer-reviewed study that says all this, although there are studies supporting various parts of it. As with any guide, see what makes sense for you, your genetics, your situation, and your experience. People are all quite different, and you never know until you try.\nThe “Biological Resilience” Protocol\nA Complete Guide to Bio-De-Armoring\n⚠ CRITICAL MEDICAL DISCLAIMER:DMSO Safety: You should use 99.9% Pharmaceutical Grade DMSO, ideally in a glass bottle. It’s sold on Amazon and other sites (I’ve never had a bad batch of DMSO). Ensure hands, lungs, and nose are clean before using. See my full DMSO reference here."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 43, 1403, 1703, "\nElectrolytes: Consult a doctor if you have kidney disease or heart conditions.\nEthnobotanicals:Iboga and Psilocybin are illegal in many jurisdictions and carry risks. Never combine Iboga with most medications (especially heart & psych meds). See full iboga guide here, and microdosing protocol here."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 49, 1703, 2050, "\nBehavioral Warning (The Isolation Trap): While this protocol demands starving the brain of “Phasic” Dopamine (excitement, novelty, the chase), do not isolate completely. Total social isolation spikes Cortisol, the chronic stress hormone, which sensitizes the brain to Glutamate and effectively locks the armor in place even without any addiction."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 27, 2050, 2240, " You need the “Oxytocinergic Anchoring” of healthy social relationships, because humans are social animals.\nThe Rule: Seek “Boring Love” (parallel play, reading next to someone, safe touch)."], ["Human Written", "Low", 28, 2240, 2414, " Avoid “Exciting Love” (romance, high-stakes drama), as this spikes Phasic Dopamine and resets the armor.\nCognitive Warning: As you de-armor, you will feel naked and exposed."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 9, 2414, 2465, " You will assume everyone can see your anxiety. Dr."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 378, 2465, 5021, " Nicholas Epley, *Mindwise*, calls this the “Illusion of Transparency.”\nThe armored brain projects its own internal threat level onto neutral faces. You will think people are judging you; in reality, they are just thinking about themselves. Rule: During this protocol, do not trust your social intuition. It is calibrated to “Threat,” not “Truth.” Assume you are misreading every room until your heart rate is below 90 BPM.\nAgmatine Warning (The Voltage Governor): Agmatine is not a basic nutrient like magnesium or a membrane nutrient like phosphatidylcholine. It is a multi-target neuromodulator that can affect NMDA/glutamate signaling, imidazoline/alpha-2 adrenergic tone, nitric-oxide pathways, and opioid reward/tolerance.\nDo not combine agmatine casually with opioids, kratom, clonidine/guanfacine, blood-pressure medication, nitrates, PDE-5 inhibitors, MAOIs, or complex psychiatric medication stacks without clinician review. Avoid it during pregnancy or breastfeeding, and be especially cautious with bipolar disorder, psychosis history, unstable panic, low blood pressure, kidney/liver disease, or active substance relapse risk.\nStop immediately if it causes flatness, anhedonia, emotional blunting, new depression, agitation, insomnia, dizziness, palpitations, nausea, loose stools, diarrhea, or increased craving. Do not “push through” numbness. If agmatine makes the world more gray, it is the wrong tool for that phase.\nUridine & 5-HTP Warning for Psychedelic Users: These are not “trip enhancers.” They are repair-oriented levers that can change brain sensitivity quickly. 5-HTP is serotonergic because it is a direct serotonin precursor. Do not combine it with SSRIs, SNRIs, MAOIs, linezolid, lithium, tramadol, methadone, fentanyl, DXM, MDMA, St. John’s wort, SAM-e, L-tryptophan, or other serotonin-raising stacks without clinician review. Be especially conservative around ayahuasca / harmalas because MAO-A inhibition can amplify serotonin load, and around iboga / ibogaine because ibogaine and noribogaine interact with serotonin transport biology and already carry serious cardiac and neurological risk.\nRule: do not take 5-HTP on the same day as psychedelics, and do not use it anywhere near ayahuasca/harmalas or iboga unless the whole medicine plan has been medically reviewed. Uridine is not serotonergic, but it may still change dream vividness, visual sensitivity, craving, and psychedelic tolerance. Do not take UMP on the same day as psychedelics; if sensitivity changes, assume your old psychedelic dose may now be too high."]]}
{"name": "n1102-02", "sha256": "5f19657e3fe897baf86a4d89edf5f6b93403c656c48e3599941663ee24fda9fd", "words": 460, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.8350645899772644, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.4122825969125653e-15, "fraction_human": 0.1649354249238968, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/4a16dcc4-4000-4e0b-a6cc-c09b9bba32d4", "utc": "2026-11-02T18:54:06Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Medium", 8, 0, 52, "Psychology is the Software; Biology is the Hardware."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 47, 52, 390, "\nStandard therapy attempts to rewrite the “code” (thoughts/behaviors) while the “motherboard” (the brain’s physical structure and chemical environment) is often overheating or damaged. The science behind this protocol focuses on four specific neuro-biological mechanisms that must be addressed before psychological tools can be effective."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 4, 390, 423, "\nThe “Underpinning” Principle Dr."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 40, 423, 692, " Bruce Perry compares treating trauma to building a house. Standard CBT & EMDR style therapies attempt to “decorate” the house (changing thoughts/behaviors in the Cortex) while the foundation (the Brainstem) is crumbling. You cannot hang curtains in a collapsing house."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 5, 692, 719, "\nThe Modern “Role-Self” vs."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 11, 719, 780, " The Ancient “True-Self”\nWhy does the brain build this armor?"], ["AI-Generated", "High", 30, 780, 989, " Psychologist Lindsay Gibson explains that *Adult children of emotionally immature parents* survive by creating a “Role-Self”—a defensive personality designed to please others and manage the parent’s emotions."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 13, 989, 1054, " But we can’t just blame our immature parents for this Role Self."], ["Human Written", "High", 32, 1054, 1227, " It really is true what they say: “It takes a village to raise a child.” The modern large society with only one or two people caring for the children is vastly insufficient."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 23, 1227, 1360, " As Dr. Bruce Perry explains, our brains evolved in hunter-gatherer bands with a ratio of 4 developmentally mature adults to 1 child."], ["Human Written", "Low", 11, 1360, 1433, " Today, our “enriched” environments offer 1 immature adult to 4 children."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 60, 1433, 1775, "\nWe are operating on less than 1/24th of the relational density our biology requires. The “Void” you feel is real. Once you have de-armored, you cannot simply return to a lonely life. You must aggressively engineer a “High-Density” social environment (A Tribe), or the brain will eventually reach for the armor again just to survive the cold."], ["Human Written", "Low", 13, 1775, 1851, "\nAs we grow up, our “Role-Self” becomes calcified by Dopamine and DeltaFosB."], ["Human Written", "Low", 4, 1851, 1872, " It becomes a prison."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 14, 1872, 1952, " Your addiction is often just the fuel required to keep the “Role-Self” running."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 26, 1952, 2117, " This protocol dissolves the chemical glue holding that false persona together, allowing your “True-Self”—the person you were before the trauma—to finally re-emerge."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 7, 2117, 2178, "\nNeurological De-Armoring is underpinning (not redecorating)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 47, 2178, 2494, " This protocol acts as a metabolic solvent—an HDAC inhibitor—that softens the neural concrete of the brainstem by modulating Glutamate and introducing Ketones (BHB). We are digging underneath the house to pour a new foundation so that, eventually, the psychological “software” updates upstairs will actually install."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 7, 2494, 2538, "\nThe Anti-Breakthrough (Micro-Dosing) As Dr."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 34, 2538, 2755, " Perry explains, we need to temporarily abandon the therapy ideal of the “hour-long breakthrough.” A sensitized, armored nervous system cannot metabolize sixty minutes of trauma processing; that is a flood, not a fix."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 2755, 2759, " Dr."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 47, 2759, 3039, " Perry’s data indicates the “therapeutic window” for a dysregulated brain is often only seconds long.\nYour goal is Micro-Dosing Safety: 30 seconds of regulated breathing, twenty times a day. We are not running a marathon; we are doing physical therapy for a broken nervous system."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 3, 3039, 3066, " Frequency beats intensity."]]}
{"name": "n1102-03", "sha256": "0bb6e8b0b914c280b6f415852dc0e8b8106195f5a01bfc4c23ad6322b2abba85", "words": 671, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.7621148228645325, "fraction_ai_assisted": 6.116073282814785e-20, "fraction_human": 0.23788520693778992, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/05f9ef76-32e6-4973-ae51-d40d14b04dbb", "utc": "2026-11-02T18:54:10Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 27, 0, 173, "Part 1: THE SCIENCE (Why We Do This)\nBefore applying the tools, you must understand the specific “Hardware Failures” that occur during trauma, withdrawal, or chronic stress."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 173, 176, "\nA."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 23, 176, 306, " The Metabolic Red Line\nWe often assume we can “think” our way out of a trigger, but data proves that anatomy overrides intellect."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 306, 310, " Dr."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 44, 310, 585, " Perry identifies a “Metabolic Red Line” for the traumatized brain: when the resting heart rate is elevated or heart-rate-variability reduced (a state of “Fear”), the brain physically shunts blood flow away from the Cortex (Logic/Reason) and down to the Brainstem (Survival)."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 7, 585, 635, "\nIn this state, functional IQ drops substantially."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 47, 635, 937, " More importantly, this state floods the Nucleus Accumbens with the exact cocktail of catecholamines that transcribes new DeltaFosB proteins (the “armor”). The Takeaway: If you attempt to process trauma while living above this red line, you are not de-armoring; you are actively re-enforcing the armor."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 937, 940, "\nB."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 15, 940, 1063, " The “Overheating” CPU: Glutamate Excitotoxicity\nThe Problem: Glutamate is the brain’s primary excitatory neurotransmitter."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 9, 1063, 1117, " In states of stress, the brain floods with Glutamate."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 54, 1117, 1475, " This is the “voltage spike”—the engine is redlining.\nThe Metabolic Red Line: We often assume we can ‘think’ our way out of trauma, but Dr. Bruce Perry’s data proves that anatomy overrides intellect. When trauma survivors become highly dysregulated, prefrontal cortical functioning often decreases while survival-oriented neural systems become more dominant."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 38, 1475, 1752, " In this state, learning and memory processes may favor reinforcement of existing fear networks rather than integration of traumatic material. For this reason many trauma therapies emphasize staying within a manageable “window of tolerance” rather than overwhelming activation."], ["Human Written", "High", 23, 1752, 1884, " You can often tell when you’re dysregulated by noticing if your heart is beating faster or if your heart-rate variability declines."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 12, 1884, 1952, " DeltaFosB may be the master switch, but the research isn’t settled."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 17, 1952, 2061, "\nThe Mechanism: Excess Glutamate over-activates NMDA receptors, acting like a key stuck in the “On” position."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 8, 2061, 2126, " This causes “excitotoxicity”—literally vibrating cells to death."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 50, 2126, 2441, " Subjectively, this feels like anxiety, rage, or an “itchy brain.”\nThe Signal Dial (GluD Receptors): Beyond the “voltage spike” of NMDA, Johns Hopkins researchers have recently discovered the brain uses GluD receptors as a master volume knob. While NMDA is the spark, GluD manages the baseline “hum” of the synapse."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 43, 2441, 2743, " In an armored state, this dial is often jammed in the “High” position (Cerebellar Ataxia/Hyper-vigilance) or “Low” (Apathy/Schizotypy).\nD-serine may support therapeutic memory updating through NMDA-dependent learning mechanisms, while also engaging GluD receptors that regulate synaptic activity/tone."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 8, 2743, 2792, " The specific drug form studied is D-cycloserine."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 18, 2792, 2923, " which has evidence as an exposure-therapy augmenter because it can facilitate NMDA-dependent consolidation of extinction learning."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 64, 2923, 3325, " It does not erase fear directly; it appears to strengthen whatever learning occurs during or after the exposure session. This is why session quality matters: if the exposure produces corrective learning and ends with reduced fear or mastery, DCS (and possibly D-serine also) may help consolidate that new memory; if the exposure is overwhelming or ends badly, it may consolidate the wrong association."], ["Human Written", "High", 82, 3325, 3824, "\nThe Fix (”Lock, Stock, and Barrel”):The Vacuum (NAC): Clears the flood by exchanging glutamate for cystine.\nThe Lock (Zinc/Magnesium): Physically blocks the receptor channel to stop the voltage.\nThe Repair (Leucine/L-Serine): L-Serine acts as a precursor to D-Serine to recalibrate the GluD ‘Volume Dial’ to enhance therapeutic sessions that end with low fear/high mastery (although conversion to D-serine is inefficient, which is why some people use D-serine itself which has higher risk/benefit)."], ["Human Written", "Low", 56, 3824, 4203, " Leucine facilitates structural repair while simultaneously tuning synaptic gain to reduce the ‘itchy brain’ sensation\nThe Governor (Agmatine): Agmatine is the optional “voltage governor.” It may help when the problem is not just excess glutamate in the synapse, but NMDA/GluN2B over-reactivity — the hot, itchy, reactive, pain-y, rumination-heavy version of the Glutamate Storm."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 33, 4203, 4386, " It is not a daily foundation nutrient. It is a state-dependent brake.\nImportant conflict: do not use agmatine as a same-session companion to D-Serine/DCS-style exposure or EMDR work."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 20, 4386, 4518, " D-Serine/DCS-style tools are meant to support NMDA-dependent learning and memory updating; agmatine partially brakes NMDA activity."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 16, 4518, 4629, " Use agmatine for storm control, not immediately before a session where the goal is deliberate reconsolidation."]]}
{"name": "n1102-04", "sha256": "9fb87b3c1b452826a3025d50e0216091808635bd4f765fdabc82f6dbd7563684", "words": 474, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 3.946818132732899e-12, "fraction_human": 1.179490194402888e-08, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/9bcacab5-ab61-4786-95d4-c2cff002314e", "utc": "2026-11-02T18:54:17Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 0, 2, "C."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 57, 2, 381, " The “Hardened” Circuit: Dynorphin & DeltaFosB\nThe Problem: To protect itself from the Glutamate storm, the brain eventually releases Dynorphin, a chemical blanket that suppresses dopamine. This creates the “Void”—a state of apathy, grayness, and an inability to feel pleasure.\nWhy Standard Meds Failed You If you have tried SSRIs (antidepressants) and failed, you are not crazy."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 30, 381, 583, " Ipser & Stein 2012 study showed that Prozac had zero effect on male combat veterans with calcified PTSD. And the side effects are well-known, including anhedonia, zombification, and sexual dysfunction."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 9, 583, 629, "\nWhy don’t these drugs work on calcified PTSD?"], ["AI-Generated", "High", 99, 629, 1289, " Because standard serotonin drugs treat the “software” (mood), but they cannot penetrate the “hardware” (the structural changes in the amygdala caused by severe trauma). This protocol uses Ketones and HDAC Inhibitors to remodel the physical structure of the brain that resists standard medication.\nThe Hardening: Chronic cycles lead to the accumulation of DeltaFosB, a protein switch that permanently alters gene expression to cement the trauma circuitry (Vialou, et al, 2010).\nThe Fix (The Unlock): You cannot “wait” for this to pass. We use “System Reformats” (Shrooms/Iboga) to stimulate GDNF, which physically rewires the brain around these hardened loops."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 1289, 1292, "\nD."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 32, 1292, 1506, " The “Lagging” System: Toxicity & Hypometabolism (The Fog)\nThe Problem: “Brain Fog” is often a fuel crisis. Trauma causes cerebral insulin resistance—your neurons are swimming in glucose (sugar) but cannot burn it."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 4, 1506, 1529, " The engine is flooded."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 30, 1529, 1703, "\nThe Fix: If the brain cannot burn sugar, we switch fuels. We use PQQ to boost ATP, and Ketones, which bypass the broken glucose pathways and enter the mitochondria directly."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 7, 1703, 1746, " This turns the lights back on immediately."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 17, 1746, 1846, " We alternate hot and cold showers to boost p131 and heat shock proteins and reduce inflammation.\nE."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 196, 1846, 3017, " The “Save Button”: Memory Reconsolidation\nThe Problem: Every time you have a flashback, your brain attempts to “save” the memory again, often reinforcing the emotional trauma loop.\nThe Fix (”The Jammer”): Memories require visual processing power to be restored. If you occupy the Visual-Spatial Working Memory (e.g., playing Tetris) during the critical window after a flashback, the brain fails to “save” the visual details. The memory is restored, but the emotional “sting” is permanently reduced.\nInstead of Tetris (which requires app/phone), you can use the “Color-Path Connect” method. This is more effective than simple counting because it forces your brain to map 3D space, which directly competes with the visual “saving” of a traumatic memory.\nHow to play:Pick a color (e.g., Blue).\nTrace a Path: Find every blue object in the room and mentally draw a line connecting them from left to right.\nAdd Complexity: Now, mentally “rotate” those objects in your mind or imagine them changing into a different shape (e.g., “That blue chair is now a blue cube”).\nThe Goal: You must do this for 10–20 minutes immediately after a trigger to “jam” the memory reconsolidation."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 3017, 3020, "\n+1"]]}
{"name": "n1102-05", "sha256": "81a8051e18ed688c99d1ea6c460aa863b13819dd023f794835cbfe8d52626a5d", "words": 532, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.9992587566375732, "fraction_ai_assisted": 2.6249922374654844e-12, "fraction_human": 0.0007412200211547315, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/5d298f8c-a8ed-4173-8077-cecef9ba6074", "utc": "2026-11-02T18:54:24Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Low", 38, 0, 264, "Part 2: Reducing Anxiety & Depression\nLower the Cortisol Floor (Phosphatidylserine)\nBefore ketones, before D-Serine, address cortisol directly — because cortisol is what sensitizes the brain to Glutamate and locks the armor in place (see the Isolation Trap above)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 46, 264, 527, " The single most useful nutrient I’ve found for this is Phosphatidylserine (PS), a phospholipid that blunts the HPA-axis cortisol response to stress.\nWho it’s for: People running high or reactive cortisol — the “wired and tired,” can’t-downshift, waking-at-3-a.m."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 527, 533, " type."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 24, 533, 687, " This includes many people with slow COMT (the Val158Met variant that clears catecholamines slowly, so stress hormones linger and you stay on high alert)."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 18, 687, 788, " One friend, Scott, with exactly this profile got more out of PS than anything else in this protocol."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 124, 788, 1507, " Be honest about the evidence, though: the cortisol-lowering effect is best documented in chronically stressed people; the slow-COMT angle is mechanism plus my own observation, not a controlled finding.\nDose: 300–600 mg/day, taken earlier in the day. Below ~300 mg the cortisol effect is unreliable; above ~800 mg adds nothing.\nFood instead of capsules: One of the few supplements you can actually eat your way to. Atlantic mackerel (~480 mg/100g) and herring (~360 mg) are richest; tuna is lower (~194 mg). A 200g mackerel fillet ≈ 960 mg PS — above clinical doses. (Don’t lean on tuna daily — mercury.)\n⚠ The catch, again: PS is only for genuinely high cortisol — and there are two ways to find out you guessed wrong."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 5, 1507, 1538, " PS works by blunting cortisol."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 185, 1538, 2585, " If yours isn’t actually elevated, lowering it pushes you down the other side of the curve, where the symptoms look almost identical to high cortisol. Watch for either signal:\nFlat / numb / no drive — you’ve over-suppressed. Classic too-little-cortisol.\nMore wired, not less — racing thoughts, 3 a.m. waking, irritability, vivid or stressful dreams. Counterintuitive but real: when cortisol drops too far, the body leans on adrenaline to hold up blood pressure and alertness, and you feel more stressed, not less.\nEither one means PS is the wrong tool for you right now. Don’t raise the dose to push through — stop. If you want to know before you start, a 4-point salivary cortisol test tells you whether you’re actually high. (A minority also report low blood pressure, water-weight gain, or restless legs — all consistent with cortisol going too low.)\nThe rule of thumb if you can’t test: Wired, tired, can’t switch off, 3 a.m. waking → probably high, PS is worth a trial. Numb, low-drive, flat → probably not high; PS will likely make it worse."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 5, 2585, 2608, " Skip it or test first."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 110, 2608, 3312, "\nAgmatine vs PS vs Phosphatidylcholine\nDo not confuse these three tools:\nPhosphatidylserine (PS) is the cortisol-floor tool. Use it only for the high-cortisol “wired and tired” profile.\nPhosphatidylcholine (PC) is a membrane/choline nutrient. It may support general cell-membrane and acetylcholine biology, but it is not a targeted cortisol-lowering or glutamate-braking intervention.\nAgmatine is different from both. It is an optional glutamate/NO/imidazoline “voltage governor.” It belongs in the Shield section, not as a replacement for PS or PC. Like PS, it can overcorrect the system: PS can push low-cortisol people into flatness; agmatine can push already-numb people into more emotional blunting."]]}
{"name": "n1102-06", "sha256": "3b8a6cced9d2dba78d565b2826308504a89df59541d1020c0c06ce4909ef7630", "words": 480, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.9173590889811453e-23, "fraction_human": 6.461370477214246e-17, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/f04ffdea-2c78-4093-883f-fdc1b287dc37", "utc": "2026-11-02T18:54:31Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 450, 0, 2899, "Dopamine Receptor Burnout / DAWS Pattern: Uridine Monophosphate\nWho this is for: This is not for everyone with depression. This is for the specific “burned-out dopamine receptor” pattern: gray anhedonia, weak dreams, weak psychedelic visuals, needing unusually high doses to feel anything, compulsive reaching for ketamine/LSD/novelty just to get a hit, and especially a history of dopamine agonist withdrawal from drugs like pramipexole or ropinirole. The medical literature calls this dopamine agonist withdrawal syndrome (DAWS), and describes anxiety, panic, dysphoria, depression, agitation, fatigue, autonomic symptoms, pain, and drug cravings after dopamine-agonist tapering. In Scott’s case, the pattern looked like DAWS with D2/D3 reward-system downregulation, then made worse by frequent LSD microdosing and ketamine attempts to force dopamine hits. That is a specific phenotype, not a generic “everyone needs dopamine” claim.\nThe tool:Uridine monophosphate (UMP). The best evidence is not “UMP cures DAWS”; that study does not exist. The evidence is more basic: uridine, choline, and DHA are circulating precursors for brain phosphatide / synaptic membrane synthesis. Wurtman’s group has shown that DHA + uridine + choline can increase synaptic membrane components and synaptic proteins, that DHA-induced dendritic spine formation is enhanced by UMP in animals, and that dietary UMP increased potassium-evoked dopamine release and neurite outgrowth in aged rats. So the mechanism is plausible, but the DAWS use is still a cautious human extrapolation plus anecdote.\nScott’s signal: Scott already had choline from eggs and DHA/EPA from fish oil. After adding standard-dose UMP, he got a striking response within a day: vivid dreams returned, real childhood memories came back in dreams, psychedelic tolerance seemed to drop, and ketamine/LSD craving fell hard. That does not prove UMP rebuilt D3 receptors overnight. It does suggest that, in the right person, UMP can be a very clean signal that the synaptic-membrane / dopamine-receptor-recovery axis was starved.\nTrial: UMP 150–300 mg in the morning with food for 3–7 days. Keep omega-3s in place, especially DHA/EPA. Make sure there is enough choline from eggs, phosphatidylcholine, CDP-choline, or another tolerated choline source. Do not start UMP on the same day you start 5-HTP, agmatine, D-serine, keto, iboga, shrooms, LSD, ketamine, or any other major variable. You are trying to see whether UMP itself changes the signal.\nSide effects / stop signs: The most common problem is the “choline headache” or spaced-out brain fog: if UMP accelerates membrane synthesis while choline availability is low, the system can feel under-supplied. Other stop signs include insomnia, jitteriness, racing thoughts, irritability, emotional flatness, nausea, stomach cramps, or loose stools. If it makes you wired, numb, or weirdly irritable, stop."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 4, 2899, 2920, " Do not push through."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 47, 2920, 3209, "\nPsychedelic caution: If UMP makes dreams vivid or suddenly lowers psychedelic tolerance, treat that as a safety signal. Do not take UMP on psychedelic days. If you use psychedelics later, assume your previous dose may be too strong and that chasing the old visual threshold can overshoot."]]}
{"name": "n1102-07", "sha256": "ae4d14fff40c5e796e219317c3df1e68238b2c399aaadb60c0151f9f39a81990", "words": 594, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.8211087584495544, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.7656360650492695e-43, "fraction_human": 0.17889124155044556, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/1239d2f8-ca44-4713-b0b7-e9791b5211e3", "utc": "2026-11-02T18:54:35Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 441, 0, 2730, "Serotonin Bottleneck Pattern: 5-HTP + Low-Dose P5P\nWho this is for: This is for the low-serotonin-looking pattern, not for every depressed person. Think poor sleep initiation, low mood, low warmth, night anxiety, repetitive rumination, and a genetic or clinical reason to suspect a bottleneck in serotonin synthesis. Scott’s genetic data suggested a TPH2 bottleneck, and 5-HTP helped his sleep and mood. If you are already agitated, manic, on serotonergic meds, or using serotonergic psychedelics/entactogens, this is not a casual experiment.\nThe tool:5-HTP bypasses the tryptophan-to-5-HTP step and gives the body a more direct serotonin precursor. A broad review of 5-HTP discusses its role in serotonin biology and its use in mood, anxiety, sleep, obesity, myoclonus, and serotonin-toxicity contexts. The evidence for depression and sleep is mixed and not as strong as people online imply, but the mechanism is real enough that responders can feel it quickly.\nScott’s version: 100 mg 5-HTP sublingually at night, with 10–20 mg P5P sublingually in the morning. The P5P is there as the active B6 cofactor for aromatic amino-acid decarboxylase, not as a stimulant. Scott is slow-COMT and sensitive to too much P5P, so the low dose matters. More is not better.\nTrial: Start lower if you are sensitive: 50 mg 5-HTP at night for 2–3 nights, then 100 mg only if the lower amount is clearly helpful and not activating. Optional P5P: 10–20 mg in the morning, especially if 5-HTP feels like it “almost works” but is not converting cleanly. Do not combine the trial with UMP, agmatine, D-serine, psychedelics, or medication changes. If it is the right tool, the first signal is usually sleep quality, dream tone, mood warmth, or reduced nighttime rumination.\nSide effects / stop signs: Nausea, stomach discomfort, loose stools, headache, vivid or intense dreams, insomnia, sweating, tremor, anxiety, irritability, emotional agitation, or a too-bright / hypomanic feeling. Stop immediately if you get agitation + sweating + diarrhea + tremor/clonus + fever, confusion, fast heart rate, or unstable blood pressure. That pattern can indicate serotonin toxicity, which can become dangerous.\nHard interaction rule: 5-HTP should not be mixed casually with serotonin-raising drugs or supplements. Case literature and clinical reviews warn about serotonin syndrome risk when 5-HTP is combined with antidepressants or MAOIs, and serotonin syndrome is most often a multi-drug / stack problem. See the dietary supplement interaction case report and the general serotonin-syndrome overview from MedlinePlus. For this readership: avoid 5-HTP on psychedelic days, and be especially strict around ayahuasca / harmala MAOI chemistry and iboga / ibogaine."], ["Human Written", "High", 80, 2730, 3209, "\nFixing ATP Signaling if Cortisol Isn’t High\nRecent neuroscience (Tian-Ming Gao, et al, 2025) has shown in male mice that anxiety and depression are a result of reduced hippocampal ATP signaling. Calabrese, et al (2024) have shown in one study that’s part of much broader research that ketones and reduced carbohydrate intake are highly effective for anxiety, depression, and other mental illnesses. To address both issues, you can trial a morning dose of 20mg of PQQand ketones."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 8, 3209, 3262, "\nKETONE DECISION: You must choose your fuel strategy."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 51, 3262, 3581, " This determines your electrolyte protocol.\nStrategy A: The “Crisis Mode” (BHB, Beta-hydroxybutyrate Salts)Method: You eat a standard low-sugar diet but drink Ketones (BHB Salts) to clear the fog.\nStrategy B: The “Resilience Mode” (Keto Diet)Method: You restrict carbs (<20g/day) to force your liver to produce Ketones."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 11, 3581, 3637, "\nFat:EAT FAT TO SATIETY. This is your new energy source."], ["Human Written", "Low", 34, 3637, 3846, " Do not rely on lean protein alone (chicken breast), or your body will convert the protein to sugar (Gluconeogenesis), keeping you out of ketosis.\nTo avoid side effects, refer to the ***Keto Adaptation Guide*."]]}
{"name": "n1102-08", "sha256": "a2d4dbfecd745fed57d21ac4f22eccc9bbce6bb86e241d77f8928d9e610fb73d", "words": 590, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.8716392517089844, "fraction_ai_assisted": 9.135236439503338e-17, "fraction_human": 0.12836074829101562, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/aa0dd77b-93d6-4bb6-b7f4-5b89d8f3f2fa", "utc": "2026-11-02T18:54:39Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 18, 0, 129, "Part 3: THE SHIELD (Flu-Proofing & Voltage Control)\nGoal: Stabilize voltage to prevent the “Biological Crash” (Headaches/Panic).\n"], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 129, 131, "1."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 260, 131, 1703, " Electrolytes (Choose Your Path)\nIf on Quick Fix, Strategy A (BHB Salts / Standard Diet):Sodium: Standard intake. DO NOT load extra salt (Risk of High Blood Pressure).\nPotassium:\nGoal: Install the “Brake Pads” for your nervous system.\nMechanism: Potassium Channels (KCNQ).\nThe Science: Your neurons have “brakes” called KCNQ channels that stop them from firing uncontrollably. These brakes run on Potassium ions. If you are low on potassium (common in high stress), your brakes fail. You can push the pedal (breathe), but the car won’t stop.\nThe Mandate: You must hit 4,700 mg of Potassium daily.\nThe Source: Food Only. (Supplements are dangerous and limited to 99mg).\nThe Menu (The “Shield” Foods):\nPotato (Baked with skin): ~925 mg (The King of Potassium).\nBeet Greens (Cooked): ~1,300 mg per cup.\nSalmon: ~1,000 mg per filet.\nAvocado: ~700-900 mg.\nCoconut Water: ~600 mg per cup.\nThe Strategy: Eat 2 large potatoes and 2 cups of greens every single day. This saturates your cells, lowering your “resting voltage” so you become physically harder to trigger.\nIf on Deep Fix, Strategy B (Keto Diet): ***See my Keto Adaptation Guide for electrolytes.***\n2. The Glutamate Shield (Anxiety):\nSulforaphane from 1 cup of broccoli sprouts (which also contain the myrosinase needed).\nFunction: It acts as a “Guardian of the Proteasome,” preventing the premature degradation of the cleanup machinery you are working so hard to build. Sulforaphane is also a potent Nrf2 activator; if you are in a “Glutamate Storm,” it helps clear oxidative stress.\nNAC: 1.8g – 2.4g (divided doses)."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 3, 1703, 1722, " Mops up glutamate."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 133, 1722, 2561, "\nAgmatine Sulfate (Optional Trial): Start with 250–500 mg in the morning or early afternoon for 3 days. If it clearly reduces the hot/itchy/reactive state without flattening mood, use 500 mg once or twice daily. For this protocol, cap at 1 g/day unless clinician-supervised.\nBest fit: Glutamate Storm + rumination/compulsion + inflammatory or neuropathic “pain-y” body state.\nPoor fit: already numb, low-drive, depressed, dissociated, low blood pressure, sedated, or entering the Dynorphin Void.\nCycle rule: use it as a 7–14 day anxiety-phase experiment, not a forever baseline. Stop if flatness, anhedonia, apathy, irritability, insomnia, dizziness, nausea, loose stools, diarrhea, or increased craving appears.\nTiming rule: avoid agmatine on D-Serine/DCS-style reconsolidation days, or keep it at least 12–24 hours away from the session."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 4, 2561, 2597, "\nMagnesium Glycinate: 400mg (Night)."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 6, 2597, 2633, " The “Plug” for the anxiety channel."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 79, 2633, 3148, "\nThe Dynorphin Bridge (Apathy / DAWS-pattern Void):Cordyceps mushrooms: A gentle vitality tool for some people, especially when the Void is mostly fatigue and low respiratory/mitochondrial drive.\nUridine Monophosphate: The more targeted option when the Void looks like dopamine-receptor burnout: low dreams, low visuals, high psychedelic tolerance, dopamine-agonist withdrawal history, or ketamine/LSD chasing. Use UMP as a 3–7 day morning trial with choline + DHA/EPA in place. Do not take it on psychedelic days.\n"], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 6, 3148, 3175, "5-HTP: Not a dopamine tool."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 30, 3175, 3388, " Use only when the parallel problem looks like low serotonin / poor sleep / TPH2 bottleneck. Do not combine with serotonergic medications, ayahuasca/harmalas, iboga, MDMA, DXM, tramadol, or same-day psychedelics.\n"], ["Human Written", "Low", 1, 3388, 3390, "3."], ["Human Written", "High", 79, 3390, 3887, " The “Nuclear Option” (Ethnobotanical)\nThe Stack: Microdose Iboga Nasal Spray (Bypasses digestion, quicker effect). Read my iboga microdosing guide to keep safe. While shrooms are often better for a functional mood brightener effect, iboga is its own kind of therapist that shows you what you need to see in a non-threatening way.\nFemale Iboga: For “Numbness/Fog” (Anima).\nMale Iboga: For “Helplessness/Relapse” (Animus).\nShrooms: Hillbilly or Mazatapec strains are some of the best (0.1g - 0.2g)."]]}
{"name": "n1102-09", "sha256": "bb36ccd80c6e19a705b1b050596b4b591735f309f13e3e64ffdd82b866a737e2", "words": 693, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.5858218669891357, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.771379442629694e-35, "fraction_human": 0.41417813301086426, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/e930f82b-3c3b-4c18-abd3-fdf75da6f2bd", "utc": "2026-11-02T18:54:46Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 173, 0, 1105, "Part 4: THE JAMMER (Acute Symptom Management)\nInstructions: When the symptom wave hits, identify the Type and apply the Fix.\nScenario A: The “Glutamate Storm”\nSymptoms: Anxiety, Rage, “Itchy” Brain, Racing Thoughts, Flashbacks.\nMechanism: The brain is firing too hot. You need to cool the system and jam the reconsolidation.\nThe Perry-Sequence (Rhythmic First, Visual Second)\nAnatomy overrides intellect. If your heart rate is elevated or heart-rate-variability (HRV) reduced significantly, your “Reasoning Brain” is offline.\nStep 1: Rhythmic Regulation (Brainstem): Perform 5 minutes of rhythmic, repetitive sensory input—walking, drumming on your thighs, or rhythmic “Therapeutic Sighing”.\nStep 2: Check Your Baseline: Once your heart rate is within normal range, you cerebral cortex is receptive. Phosphatidylserine (PS, see Part 2) is a daily baseline agent that lowers how often and how hard these storms hit; it’s not an in-the-moment tool.\nStep 3: Apply the Jammer: Now use Tetris or the “Color-Path Connect” game to overwrite the visual memory\nAdvanced tactic: The D-Serine Memory Re-consolidator."], ["Human Written", "High", 162, 1105, 2033, " While L-Serine provides the building blocks for myelin, taking D-Serine (700mg–1400mg) on an empty stomach 45 minutes before a de-armoring session acts as a “memory (re)consolidator” which can cement the benefits of therapies like EMDR which aim to rewire the affective tone of memories.\nD-serine has shown efficacy in studies where it was used to augment exposure therapy for treating a variety of conditions such as social anxiety, PTSD, and fear of public speaking. The idea is that it facilitates the consolidation of the newly formed memory of how the anticipated negative consequences of the exposure to what you fear didn’t actually happen. Some studies ssuggested that d-serine is more effective at this when the practice exposure to what you fear ends on a positive note as opposed to a negative one. Again, all d-serine is doing is making it easier to consolidate the memory of the experience into a long-term memory."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 23, 2033, 2183, "\nUse L-Serine for daily maintenance and background hardware support.\nUse D-Serine for acute sessions where you need to “force” memory reconsolidation."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 4, 2183, 2208, " Best price from LifeLab."], ["Human Written", "High", 25, 2208, 2335, " You should take it 45 minutes or so after taking PQQ & Ketones so that your brain is fueled when the GluD dial is turned down."], ["Human Written", "Low", 41, 2335, 2559, "\nWarning: Direct D-Serine carries a higher renal (kidney) load than L-Serine. Do not exceed 30mg/kg and ensure high water intake. This risk is compounded by the higher renal load caused by a keto diet or high protein intake."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 17, 2559, 2700, "\nScenario B: The “Fog”\nSymptoms: Confusion, Disassociation, Low Energy, “Lagging.”\nMechanism: Hypometabolism (Low Fuel) or Toxicity (Static)."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 26, 2700, 2859, "\nScenario C: The “Void”\nSymptoms: Numbness, Boredom, “I want to Relapse.”\nMechanism: The Dynorphin block is active. You feel “dead.” You need to force a spark."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 68, 2859, 3239, " We will utilize the science of hot and cold showers as a vascular pump, and plant medicine as needed:\nFirst-Line Void Add-Ons: If the Void has a DAWS / D2-D3 burnout flavor, trial UMP before chasing more stimulation. If the Void is mainly sleep + serotonin bottleneck, trial 5-HTP at night. Do not start both together, and do not use either to force stronger psychedelic effects."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 27, 3239, 3408, "\nHot (3 Minutes): As hot as you can safely handle. This relaxes muscles and induces mild hyperthermia, signaling the body to start producing repair proteins (HSPs/PI31)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 50, 3408, 3683, "\nThe Metabolic Red Line: If your resting heart rate is elevated or HRV reduced, do NOT use high heat yet. Heat mimics exercise and will raise your heart rate further, which can re-enforce your “armor”. Stick to lukewarm-to-cold until your baseline heart rate is below 90 BPM."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 8, 3683, 3721, "\nCold (1 Minute): Turn it to max cold."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 14, 3721, 3810, " This provides the acute stress spike needed to activate the transport motors (p38 MAPK)."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 5, 3810, 3835, "\nRepeat: Do this 3 times."], ["Human Written", "Low", 4, 3835, 3855, " Always end on cold."], ["Human Written", "High", 23, 3855, 4005, "\nFun with fungi: If the showers aren’t enough, you can microdose Hillbilly or Mazatapec (balanced, happy, spiritual) shroom strains (100-300mg daily)."], ["Human Written", "Low", 10, 4005, 4070, " This stimulates 5-HT2A receptors to bypass the “numb” receptors."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 17, 4070, 4172, "\nActivate the “Inner Father”: If you are lacking discipline, try a male iboga nasal spray micro-dose. "], ["Human Written", "High", 26, 4172, 4310, "1 spray (equal to about 150mg of bark) in the morning, as it lasts 12 hours. Make sure to check all the dangerous iboga drug interactions."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 4, 4310, 4333, " Full iboga guide here."]]}
{"name": "n1102-10", "sha256": "57120712add75f549784c0e2275781bf4dadacb0b5f82973dcf3d7fd5e3f46a2", "words": 594, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.758625328540802, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.2185388463681503e-23, "fraction_human": 0.2413746863603592, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/af13b2b1-6564-46c2-b5ac-75d87c26dd77", "utc": "2026-11-02T18:54:54Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Medium", 26, 0, 153, "Part 5: THE TIMELINE (The 8-Week Path)\nWeeks 1–2: The Glutamate Storm (Anxiety Phase)Protocol:Self-care: Hot & cold showers, alternating, ending on cold."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 12, 153, 226, " No hot showers if heart rate elevated or heart-rate-variability reduced."], ["Human Written", "High", 33, 226, 414, "\nSupplement daily:\nPhosphatidylserine 300–600 mg earlier in the day only if you fit the high-cortisol profile + 1 cup broccoli sprouts + Magnesium Glycinate 400 mg + NAC 1.8–2.4 g divided."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 95, 414, 955, "\nOptional add-on: Agmatine Sulfate 250–500 mg AM, increasing to 500 mg twice daily only if it clearly reduces the hot/itchy/reactive state without flattening mood. Cap at 1 g/day in this protocol. Do not add agmatine on the same day you increase PS, start D-Serine, change NAC dose, begin keto, microdose, or introduce any other major variable.\nIf PS leaves you flat OR more wired, you’re not a high-cortisol responder — drop it. If agmatine leaves you flat, anhedonic, dizzy, nauseous, sleepless, irritable, or more craving-prone — drop it."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 49, 955, 1247, "\nFuel: Start with BHB Salts (Strategy A) to manage initial fog.\nRescue: “The Fire” + Chantress Seba or other music + The Repair Stack (Zn/Leu/Ser) + Tetris/Color Path for acute attacks.\nWeeks 3–5: The Dynorphin Void (Depression Phase)State: The anxiety stops, but the world turns gray/boring."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 5, 1247, 1291, "\nProtocol:Taper off Phosphatidylserine here."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 221, 1291, 2583, " This phase is low-drive and gray by design — you do not want to keep blunting cortisol in an already-flattened system, or you’ll deepen the numbness. PS was for the anxiety phase; the Void phase needs the opposite. (If you never felt the wired/high-cortisol state in Weeks 1–2, you probably shouldn’t have been on PS at all.)\nAlso stop agmatine here unless it is unmistakably helping acute glutamate storms without worsening flatness. The Void phase is already low-drive and gray; agmatine can over-brake the system in the same direction.\nUMP trial if the Void looks like DAWS: 150–300 mg UMP in the morning with food for 3–7 days, with choline + DHA/EPA in place. Best fit: low dreams, weak visuals, high psychedelic tolerance, dopamine-agonist withdrawal history, ketamine/LSD craving, or dopamine-hit chasing. Do not take UMP on psychedelic days, and assume old psychedelic doses may become too strong if sensitivity returns.\n5-HTP trial if the bottleneck looks serotonergic: 50–100 mg at night for 2–3 nights, with optional P5P 10–20 mg in the morning. Best fit: poor sleep, low mood warmth, nighttime rumination, or TPH2-style serotonin synthesis bottleneck. Do not use with serotonergic medications/supplements, ayahuasca/harmalas, iboga, MDMA, DXM, tramadol, or same-day psychedelics."], ["Human Written", "Low", 7, 2583, 2633, "\nHot & cold showers, alternating, ending on cold)."], ["Human Written", "High", 12, 2633, 2706, " No hot showers if heart rate elevated or heart-rate-variability reduced."], ["Human Written", "Low", 15, 2706, 2803, " Reduce or stop phosphatidylserine here — you don’t want to suppress an already-flattened system."], ["Human Written", "High", 52, 2803, 3126, " Micro-dose Male Iboga (if heart is ok).\nTransition: Consider moving to Strategy B (Keto Diet) for long-term repair (Autophagy) now that the acute storm has passed.\nRescue:\nIf Foggy: Inhale DMSO + Drink BHB.\nIf Numb: Micro-dose Male Iboga and/or Hillybilly/Mazatapec shrooms.\nWeek 8+: The BaselineState: DeltaFosB degraded."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 14, 3126, 3238, " Hardware reset complete.\nMaintenance: Cycle off NAC. Maintain metabolic flexibility (Low Carb/Seasonally Keto)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 51, 3238, 3536, "\nThe Aftermath: The Relational Vacuum\nAs the armor decays, you will experience a frightening but beautiful side effect: Interoception. Van der Kolk describes this as the ability to “feel” your own body again. For years, you have likely been numb—living in your head to avoid the pain in your chest."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 25, 3536, 3663, "\nAs the dopamine armor fades, you will feel your heart beat. You will feel your gut churn. You will feel the wind on your skin."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 7, 3663, 3708, " Do not mistake this sensitivity for anxiety."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 16, 3708, 3783, " It is not a symptom of sickness; it is the symptom of coming back to life."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 2, 3783, 3795, " Welcome it."]]}
{"name": "n1102-whole", "sha256": "96c80da07b3945f2b628bdffdfa90c83681e49e7a033b7e2007b9eb2928480b6", "words": 5821, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.833358883857727, "fraction_ai_assisted": 3.922632025107767e-15, "fraction_human": 0.16664110124111176, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/72952f09-0e99-46d6-b89f-5fa574422584", "utc": "2026-11-02T18:55:05Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 228, 0, 1403, "Introduction\nWhen people tell me they have trauma, I generally recommend they follow my inner child therapy guide, which includes somatic therapy & breathwork. To help people engage more deeply with the practices, I have advised the use of my Ultimate Psychedelic protocol. But recently, I realized that there’s some more basic physiological interventions we need to implement before getting to those levels. The very first step is fixing your physical health and neuro-inflammation. I suggest starting with my detox guide. After addressing overall health and neuro-inflammation, this de-armoring guide gets more specific to address the hardened neural pathways that have developed over a lifetime.\nThis protocol is partly theoretical and partly based on experience reports. There’s no peer-reviewed study that says all this, although there are studies supporting various parts of it. As with any guide, see what makes sense for you, your genetics, your situation, and your experience. People are all quite different, and you never know until you try.\nThe “Biological Resilience” Protocol\nA Complete Guide to Bio-De-Armoring\n⚠ CRITICAL MEDICAL DISCLAIMER:DMSO Safety: You should use 99.9% Pharmaceutical Grade DMSO, ideally in a glass bottle. It’s sold on Amazon and other sites (I’ve never had a bad batch of DMSO). Ensure hands, lungs, and nose are clean before using. See my full DMSO reference here."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 43, 1403, 1703, "\nElectrolytes: Consult a doctor if you have kidney disease or heart conditions.\nEthnobotanicals:Iboga and Psilocybin are illegal in many jurisdictions and carry risks. Never combine Iboga with most medications (especially heart & psych meds). See full iboga guide here, and microdosing protocol here."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 49, 1703, 2050, "\nBehavioral Warning (The Isolation Trap): While this protocol demands starving the brain of “Phasic” Dopamine (excitement, novelty, the chase), do not isolate completely. Total social isolation spikes Cortisol, the chronic stress hormone, which sensitizes the brain to Glutamate and effectively locks the armor in place even without any addiction."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 14, 2050, 2157, " You need the “Oxytocinergic Anchoring” of healthy social relationships, because humans are social animals."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 13, 2157, 2240, "\nThe Rule: Seek “Boring Love” (parallel play, reading next to someone, safe touch)."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 28, 2240, 2414, " Avoid “Exciting Love” (romance, high-stakes drama), as this spikes Phasic Dopamine and resets the armor.\nCognitive Warning: As you de-armor, you will feel naked and exposed."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 9, 2414, 2465, " You will assume everyone can see your anxiety. Dr."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 378, 2465, 5021, " Nicholas Epley, *Mindwise*, calls this the “Illusion of Transparency.”\nThe armored brain projects its own internal threat level onto neutral faces. You will think people are judging you; in reality, they are just thinking about themselves. Rule: During this protocol, do not trust your social intuition. It is calibrated to “Threat,” not “Truth.” Assume you are misreading every room until your heart rate is below 90 BPM.\nAgmatine Warning (The Voltage Governor): Agmatine is not a basic nutrient like magnesium or a membrane nutrient like phosphatidylcholine. It is a multi-target neuromodulator that can affect NMDA/glutamate signaling, imidazoline/alpha-2 adrenergic tone, nitric-oxide pathways, and opioid reward/tolerance.\nDo not combine agmatine casually with opioids, kratom, clonidine/guanfacine, blood-pressure medication, nitrates, PDE-5 inhibitors, MAOIs, or complex psychiatric medication stacks without clinician review. Avoid it during pregnancy or breastfeeding, and be especially cautious with bipolar disorder, psychosis history, unstable panic, low blood pressure, kidney/liver disease, or active substance relapse risk.\nStop immediately if it causes flatness, anhedonia, emotional blunting, new depression, agitation, insomnia, dizziness, palpitations, nausea, loose stools, diarrhea, or increased craving. Do not “push through” numbness. If agmatine makes the world more gray, it is the wrong tool for that phase.\nUridine & 5-HTP Warning for Psychedelic Users: These are not “trip enhancers.” They are repair-oriented levers that can change brain sensitivity quickly. 5-HTP is serotonergic because it is a direct serotonin precursor. Do not combine it with SSRIs, SNRIs, MAOIs, linezolid, lithium, tramadol, methadone, fentanyl, DXM, MDMA, St. John’s wort, SAM-e, L-tryptophan, or other serotonin-raising stacks without clinician review. Be especially conservative around ayahuasca / harmalas because MAO-A inhibition can amplify serotonin load, and around iboga / ibogaine because ibogaine and noribogaine interact with serotonin transport biology and already carry serious cardiac and neurological risk.\nRule: do not take 5-HTP on the same day as psychedelics, and do not use it anywhere near ayahuasca/harmalas or iboga unless the whole medicine plan has been medically reviewed. Uridine is not serotonergic, but it may still change dream vividness, visual sensitivity, craving, and psychedelic tolerance. Do not take UMP on the same day as psychedelics; if sensitivity changes, assume your old psychedelic dose may now be too high."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 8, 5021, 5074, "\nPsychology is the Software; Biology is the Hardware."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 47, 5074, 5412, "\nStandard therapy attempts to rewrite the “code” (thoughts/behaviors) while the “motherboard” (the brain’s physical structure and chemical environment) is often overheating or damaged. The science behind this protocol focuses on four specific neuro-biological mechanisms that must be addressed before psychological tools can be effective."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 36, 5412, 5666, "\nThe “Underpinning” Principle Dr. Bruce Perry compares treating trauma to building a house. Standard CBT & EMDR style therapies attempt to “decorate” the house (changing thoughts/behaviors in the Cortex) while the foundation (the Brainstem) is crumbling."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 8, 5666, 5714, " You cannot hang curtains in a collapsing house."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 5, 5714, 5741, "\nThe Modern “Role-Self” vs."], ["Human Written", "Low", 11, 5741, 5802, " The Ancient “True-Self”\nWhy does the brain build this armor?"], ["Human Written", "Low", 30, 5802, 6011, " Psychologist Lindsay Gibson explains that *Adult children of emotionally immature parents* survive by creating a “Role-Self”—a defensive personality designed to please others and manage the parent’s emotions."], ["Human Written", "High", 45, 6011, 6249, " But we can’t just blame our immature parents for this Role Self. It really is true what they say: “It takes a village to raise a child.” The modern large society with only one or two people caring for the children is vastly insufficient."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 2, 6249, 6256, " As Dr."], ["Human Written", "High", 21, 6256, 6382, " Bruce Perry explains, our brains evolved in hunter-gatherer bands with a ratio of 4 developmentally mature adults to 1 child."], ["Human Written", "Low", 11, 6382, 6455, " Today, our “enriched” environments offer 1 immature adult to 4 children."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 15, 6455, 6540, "\nWe are operating on less than 1/24th of the relational density our biology requires."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 19, 6540, 6638, " The “Void” you feel is real. Once you have de-armored, you cannot simply return to a lonely life."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 26, 6638, 6797, " You must aggressively engineer a “High-Density” social environment (A Tribe), or the brain will eventually reach for the armor again just to survive the cold."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 13, 6797, 6873, "\nAs we grow up, our “Role-Self” becomes calcified by Dopamine and DeltaFosB."], ["Human Written", "Low", 4, 6873, 6894, " It becomes a prison."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 14, 6894, 6974, " Your addiction is often just the fuel required to keep the “Role-Self” running."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 121, 6974, 7777, " This protocol dissolves the chemical glue holding that false persona together, allowing your “True-Self”—the person you were before the trauma—to finally re-emerge.\nNeurological De-Armoring is underpinning (not redecorating). This protocol acts as a metabolic solvent—an HDAC inhibitor—that softens the neural concrete of the brainstem by modulating Glutamate and introducing Ketones (BHB). We are digging underneath the house to pour a new foundation so that, eventually, the psychological “software” updates upstairs will actually install.\nThe Anti-Breakthrough (Micro-Dosing) As Dr. Perry explains, we need to temporarily abandon the therapy ideal of the “hour-long breakthrough.” A sensitized, armored nervous system cannot metabolize sixty minutes of trauma processing; that is a flood, not a fix."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 7777, 7781, " Dr."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 47, 7781, 8061, " Perry’s data indicates the “therapeutic window” for a dysregulated brain is often only seconds long.\nYour goal is Micro-Dosing Safety: 30 seconds of regulated breathing, twenty times a day. We are not running a marathon; we are doing physical therapy for a broken nervous system."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 3, 8061, 8088, " Frequency beats intensity."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 27, 8088, 8262, "\nPart 1: THE SCIENCE (Why We Do This)\nBefore applying the tools, you must understand the specific “Hardware Failures” that occur during trauma, withdrawal, or chronic stress."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 8262, 8265, "\nA."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 23, 8265, 8395, " The Metabolic Red Line\nWe often assume we can “think” our way out of a trigger, but data proves that anatomy overrides intellect."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 8395, 8399, " Dr."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 98, 8399, 9026, " Perry identifies a “Metabolic Red Line” for the traumatized brain: when the resting heart rate is elevated or heart-rate-variability reduced (a state of “Fear”), the brain physically shunts blood flow away from the Cortex (Logic/Reason) and down to the Brainstem (Survival).\nIn this state, functional IQ drops substantially. More importantly, this state floods the Nucleus Accumbens with the exact cocktail of catecholamines that transcribes new DeltaFosB proteins (the “armor”). The Takeaway: If you attempt to process trauma while living above this red line, you are not de-armoring; you are actively re-enforcing the armor."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 9026, 9029, "\nB."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 33, 9029, 9259, " The “Overheating” CPU: Glutamate Excitotoxicity\nThe Problem: Glutamate is the brain’s primary excitatory neurotransmitter. In states of stress, the brain floods with Glutamate. This is the “voltage spike”—the engine is redlining."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 17, 9259, 9345, "\nThe Metabolic Red Line: We often assume we can ‘think’ our way out of trauma, but Dr."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 9, 9345, 9405, " Bruce Perry’s data proves that anatomy overrides intellect."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 57, 9405, 9841, " When trauma survivors become highly dysregulated, prefrontal cortical functioning often decreases while survival-oriented neural systems become more dominant. In this state, learning and memory processes may favor reinforcement of existing fear networks rather than integration of traumatic material. For this reason many trauma therapies emphasize staying within a manageable “window of tolerance” rather than overwhelming activation."], ["Human Written", "High", 23, 9841, 9973, " You can often tell when you’re dysregulated by noticing if your heart is beating faster or if your heart-rate variability declines."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 12, 9973, 10041, " DeltaFosB may be the master switch, but the research isn’t settled."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 17, 10041, 10150, "\nThe Mechanism: Excess Glutamate over-activates NMDA receptors, acting like a key stuck in the “On” position."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 8, 10150, 10215, " This causes “excitotoxicity”—literally vibrating cells to death."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 50, 10215, 10530, " Subjectively, this feels like anxiety, rage, or an “itchy brain.”\nThe Signal Dial (GluD Receptors): Beyond the “voltage spike” of NMDA, Johns Hopkins researchers have recently discovered the brain uses GluD receptors as a master volume knob. While NMDA is the spark, GluD manages the baseline “hum” of the synapse."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 21, 10530, 10666, " In an armored state, this dial is often jammed in the “High” position (Cerebellar Ataxia/Hyper-vigilance) or “Low” (Apathy/Schizotypy)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 22, 10666, 10832, "\nD-serine may support therapeutic memory updating through NMDA-dependent learning mechanisms, while also engaging GluD receptors that regulate synaptic activity/tone."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 8, 10832, 10881, " The specific drug form studied is D-cycloserine."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 82, 10881, 11414, " which has evidence as an exposure-therapy augmenter because it can facilitate NMDA-dependent consolidation of extinction learning. It does not erase fear directly; it appears to strengthen whatever learning occurs during or after the exposure session. This is why session quality matters: if the exposure produces corrective learning and ends with reduced fear or mastery, DCS (and possibly D-serine also) may help consolidate that new memory; if the exposure is overwhelming or ends badly, it may consolidate the wrong association."], ["Human Written", "High", 82, 11414, 11913, "\nThe Fix (”Lock, Stock, and Barrel”):The Vacuum (NAC): Clears the flood by exchanging glutamate for cystine.\nThe Lock (Zinc/Magnesium): Physically blocks the receptor channel to stop the voltage.\nThe Repair (Leucine/L-Serine): L-Serine acts as a precursor to D-Serine to recalibrate the GluD ‘Volume Dial’ to enhance therapeutic sessions that end with low fear/high mastery (although conversion to D-serine is inefficient, which is why some people use D-serine itself which has higher risk/benefit)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 56, 11913, 12292, " Leucine facilitates structural repair while simultaneously tuning synaptic gain to reduce the ‘itchy brain’ sensation\nThe Governor (Agmatine): Agmatine is the optional “voltage governor.” It may help when the problem is not just excess glutamate in the synapse, but NMDA/GluN2B over-reactivity — the hot, itchy, reactive, pain-y, rumination-heavy version of the Glutamate Storm."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 13, 12292, 12362, " It is not a daily foundation nutrient. It is a state-dependent brake."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 56, 12362, 12718, "\nImportant conflict: do not use agmatine as a same-session companion to D-Serine/DCS-style exposure or EMDR work. D-Serine/DCS-style tools are meant to support NMDA-dependent learning and memory updating; agmatine partially brakes NMDA activity. Use agmatine for storm control, not immediately before a session where the goal is deliberate reconsolidation."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 12718, 12721, "\nC."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 25, 12721, 12910, " The “Hardened” Circuit: Dynorphin & DeltaFosB\nThe Problem: To protect itself from the Glutamate storm, the brain eventually releases Dynorphin, a chemical blanket that suppresses dopamine."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 15, 12910, 12998, " This creates the “Void”—a state of apathy, grayness, and an inability to feel pleasure."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 17, 12998, 13100, "\nWhy Standard Meds Failed You If you have tried SSRIs (antidepressants) and failed, you are not crazy."], ["Human Written", "Low", 30, 13100, 13302, " Ipser & Stein 2012 study showed that Prozac had zero effect on male combat veterans with calcified PTSD. And the side effects are well-known, including anhedonia, zombification, and sexual dysfunction."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 9, 13302, 13348, "\nWhy don’t these drugs work on calcified PTSD?"], ["AI-Generated", "High", 99, 13348, 14008, " Because standard serotonin drugs treat the “software” (mood), but they cannot penetrate the “hardware” (the structural changes in the amygdala caused by severe trauma). This protocol uses Ketones and HDAC Inhibitors to remodel the physical structure of the brain that resists standard medication.\nThe Hardening: Chronic cycles lead to the accumulation of DeltaFosB, a protein switch that permanently alters gene expression to cement the trauma circuitry (Vialou, et al, 2010).\nThe Fix (The Unlock): You cannot “wait” for this to pass. We use “System Reformats” (Shrooms/Iboga) to stimulate GDNF, which physically rewires the brain around these hardened loops."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 14008, 14011, "\nD."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 32, 14011, 14225, " The “Lagging” System: Toxicity & Hypometabolism (The Fog)\nThe Problem: “Brain Fog” is often a fuel crisis. Trauma causes cerebral insulin resistance—your neurons are swimming in glucose (sugar) but cannot burn it."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 4, 14225, 14248, " The engine is flooded."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 30, 14248, 14422, "\nThe Fix: If the brain cannot burn sugar, we switch fuels. We use PQQ to boost ATP, and Ketones, which bypass the broken glucose pathways and enter the mitochondria directly."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 23, 14422, 14562, " This turns the lights back on immediately. We alternate hot and cold showers to boost p131 and heat shock proteins and reduce inflammation."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 14562, 14565, "\nE."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 77, 14565, 15064, " The “Save Button”: Memory Reconsolidation\nThe Problem: Every time you have a flashback, your brain attempts to “save” the memory again, often reinforcing the emotional trauma loop.\nThe Fix (”The Jammer”): Memories require visual processing power to be restored. If you occupy the Visual-Spatial Working Memory (e.g., playing Tetris) during the critical window after a flashback, the brain fails to “save” the visual details. The memory is restored, but the emotional “sting” is permanently reduced."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 15, 15064, 15155, "\nInstead of Tetris (which requires app/phone), you can use the “Color-Path Connect” method."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 189, 15155, 16267, " This is more effective than simple counting because it forces your brain to map 3D space, which directly competes with the visual “saving” of a traumatic memory.\nHow to play:Pick a color (e.g., Blue).\nTrace a Path: Find every blue object in the room and mentally draw a line connecting them from left to right.\nAdd Complexity: Now, mentally “rotate” those objects in your mind or imagine them changing into a different shape (e.g., “That blue chair is now a blue cube”).\nThe Goal: You must do this for 10–20 minutes immediately after a trigger to “jam” the memory reconsolidation.\n+1\nPart 2: Reducing Anxiety & Depression\nLower the Cortisol Floor (Phosphatidylserine)\nBefore ketones, before D-Serine, address cortisol directly — because cortisol is what sensitizes the brain to Glutamate and locks the armor in place (see the Isolation Trap above). The single most useful nutrient I’ve found for this is Phosphatidylserine (PS), a phospholipid that blunts the HPA-axis cortisol response to stress.\nWho it’s for: People running high or reactive cortisol — the “wired and tired,” can’t-downshift, waking-at-3-a.m."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 16267, 16273, " type."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 921, 16273, 21952, " This includes many people with slow COMT (the Val158Met variant that clears catecholamines slowly, so stress hormones linger and you stay on high alert). One friend, Scott, with exactly this profile got more out of PS than anything else in this protocol. Be honest about the evidence, though: the cortisol-lowering effect is best documented in chronically stressed people; the slow-COMT angle is mechanism plus my own observation, not a controlled finding.\nDose: 300–600 mg/day, taken earlier in the day. Below ~300 mg the cortisol effect is unreliable; above ~800 mg adds nothing.\nFood instead of capsules: One of the few supplements you can actually eat your way to. Atlantic mackerel (~480 mg/100g) and herring (~360 mg) are richest; tuna is lower (~194 mg). A 200g mackerel fillet ≈ 960 mg PS — above clinical doses. (Don’t lean on tuna daily — mercury.)\n⚠ The catch, again: PS is only for genuinely high cortisol — and there are two ways to find out you guessed wrong. PS works by blunting cortisol. If yours isn’t actually elevated, lowering it pushes you down the other side of the curve, where the symptoms look almost identical to high cortisol. Watch for either signal:\nFlat / numb / no drive — you’ve over-suppressed. Classic too-little-cortisol.\nMore wired, not less — racing thoughts, 3 a.m. waking, irritability, vivid or stressful dreams. Counterintuitive but real: when cortisol drops too far, the body leans on adrenaline to hold up blood pressure and alertness, and you feel more stressed, not less.\nEither one means PS is the wrong tool for you right now. Don’t raise the dose to push through — stop. If you want to know before you start, a 4-point salivary cortisol test tells you whether you’re actually high. (A minority also report low blood pressure, water-weight gain, or restless legs — all consistent with cortisol going too low.)\nThe rule of thumb if you can’t test: Wired, tired, can’t switch off, 3 a.m. waking → probably high, PS is worth a trial. Numb, low-drive, flat → probably not high; PS will likely make it worse. Skip it or test first.\nAgmatine vs PS vs Phosphatidylcholine\nDo not confuse these three tools:\nPhosphatidylserine (PS) is the cortisol-floor tool. Use it only for the high-cortisol “wired and tired” profile.\nPhosphatidylcholine (PC) is a membrane/choline nutrient. It may support general cell-membrane and acetylcholine biology, but it is not a targeted cortisol-lowering or glutamate-braking intervention.\nAgmatine is different from both. It is an optional glutamate/NO/imidazoline “voltage governor.” It belongs in the Shield section, not as a replacement for PS or PC. Like PS, it can overcorrect the system: PS can push low-cortisol people into flatness; agmatine can push already-numb people into more emotional blunting.\nDopamine Receptor Burnout / DAWS Pattern: Uridine Monophosphate\nWho this is for: This is not for everyone with depression. This is for the specific “burned-out dopamine receptor” pattern: gray anhedonia, weak dreams, weak psychedelic visuals, needing unusually high doses to feel anything, compulsive reaching for ketamine/LSD/novelty just to get a hit, and especially a history of dopamine agonist withdrawal from drugs like pramipexole or ropinirole. The medical literature calls this dopamine agonist withdrawal syndrome (DAWS), and describes anxiety, panic, dysphoria, depression, agitation, fatigue, autonomic symptoms, pain, and drug cravings after dopamine-agonist tapering. In Scott’s case, the pattern looked like DAWS with D2/D3 reward-system downregulation, then made worse by frequent LSD microdosing and ketamine attempts to force dopamine hits. That is a specific phenotype, not a generic “everyone needs dopamine” claim.\nThe tool:Uridine monophosphate (UMP). The best evidence is not “UMP cures DAWS”; that study does not exist. The evidence is more basic: uridine, choline, and DHA are circulating precursors for brain phosphatide / synaptic membrane synthesis. Wurtman’s group has shown that DHA + uridine + choline can increase synaptic membrane components and synaptic proteins, that DHA-induced dendritic spine formation is enhanced by UMP in animals, and that dietary UMP increased potassium-evoked dopamine release and neurite outgrowth in aged rats. So the mechanism is plausible, but the DAWS use is still a cautious human extrapolation plus anecdote.\nScott’s signal: Scott already had choline from eggs and DHA/EPA from fish oil. After adding standard-dose UMP, he got a striking response within a day: vivid dreams returned, real childhood memories came back in dreams, psychedelic tolerance seemed to drop, and ketamine/LSD craving fell hard. That does not prove UMP rebuilt D3 receptors overnight. It does suggest that, in the right person, UMP can be a very clean signal that the synaptic-membrane / dopamine-receptor-recovery axis was starved.\nTrial: UMP 150–300 mg in the morning with food for 3–7 days. Keep omega-3s in place, especially DHA/EPA. Make sure there is enough choline from eggs, phosphatidylcholine, CDP-choline, or another tolerated choline source. Do not start UMP on the same day you start 5-HTP, agmatine, D-serine, keto, iboga, shrooms, LSD, ketamine, or any other major variable. You are trying to see whether UMP itself changes the signal.\nSide effects / stop signs: The most common problem is the “choline headache” or spaced-out brain fog: if UMP accelerates membrane synthesis while choline availability is low, the system can feel under-supplied. Other stop signs include insomnia, jitteriness, racing thoughts, irritability, emotional flatness, nausea, stomach cramps, or loose stools. If it makes you wired, numb, or weirdly irritable, stop."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 4, 21952, 21973, " Do not push through."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 488, 21973, 24993, "\nPsychedelic caution: If UMP makes dreams vivid or suddenly lowers psychedelic tolerance, treat that as a safety signal. Do not take UMP on psychedelic days. If you use psychedelics later, assume your previous dose may be too strong and that chasing the old visual threshold can overshoot.\nSerotonin Bottleneck Pattern: 5-HTP + Low-Dose P5P\nWho this is for: This is for the low-serotonin-looking pattern, not for every depressed person. Think poor sleep initiation, low mood, low warmth, night anxiety, repetitive rumination, and a genetic or clinical reason to suspect a bottleneck in serotonin synthesis. Scott’s genetic data suggested a TPH2 bottleneck, and 5-HTP helped his sleep and mood. If you are already agitated, manic, on serotonergic meds, or using serotonergic psychedelics/entactogens, this is not a casual experiment.\nThe tool:5-HTP bypasses the tryptophan-to-5-HTP step and gives the body a more direct serotonin precursor. A broad review of 5-HTP discusses its role in serotonin biology and its use in mood, anxiety, sleep, obesity, myoclonus, and serotonin-toxicity contexts. The evidence for depression and sleep is mixed and not as strong as people online imply, but the mechanism is real enough that responders can feel it quickly.\nScott’s version: 100 mg 5-HTP sublingually at night, with 10–20 mg P5P sublingually in the morning. The P5P is there as the active B6 cofactor for aromatic amino-acid decarboxylase, not as a stimulant. Scott is slow-COMT and sensitive to too much P5P, so the low dose matters. More is not better.\nTrial: Start lower if you are sensitive: 50 mg 5-HTP at night for 2–3 nights, then 100 mg only if the lower amount is clearly helpful and not activating. Optional P5P: 10–20 mg in the morning, especially if 5-HTP feels like it “almost works” but is not converting cleanly. Do not combine the trial with UMP, agmatine, D-serine, psychedelics, or medication changes. If it is the right tool, the first signal is usually sleep quality, dream tone, mood warmth, or reduced nighttime rumination.\nSide effects / stop signs: Nausea, stomach discomfort, loose stools, headache, vivid or intense dreams, insomnia, sweating, tremor, anxiety, irritability, emotional agitation, or a too-bright / hypomanic feeling. Stop immediately if you get agitation + sweating + diarrhea + tremor/clonus + fever, confusion, fast heart rate, or unstable blood pressure. That pattern can indicate serotonin toxicity, which can become dangerous.\nHard interaction rule: 5-HTP should not be mixed casually with serotonin-raising drugs or supplements. Case literature and clinical reviews warn about serotonin syndrome risk when 5-HTP is combined with antidepressants or MAOIs, and serotonin syndrome is most often a multi-drug / stack problem. See the dietary supplement interaction case report and the general serotonin-syndrome overview from MedlinePlus. For this readership: avoid 5-HTP on psychedelic days, and be especially strict around ayahuasca / harmala MAOI chemistry and iboga / ibogaine."], ["Human Written", "High", 80, 24993, 25472, "\nFixing ATP Signaling if Cortisol Isn’t High\nRecent neuroscience (Tian-Ming Gao, et al, 2025) has shown in male mice that anxiety and depression are a result of reduced hippocampal ATP signaling. Calabrese, et al (2024) have shown in one study that’s part of much broader research that ketones and reduced carbohydrate intake are highly effective for anxiety, depression, and other mental illnesses. To address both issues, you can trial a morning dose of 20mg of PQQand ketones."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 8, 25472, 25525, "\nKETONE DECISION: You must choose your fuel strategy."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 51, 25525, 25844, " This determines your electrolyte protocol.\nStrategy A: The “Crisis Mode” (BHB, Beta-hydroxybutyrate Salts)Method: You eat a standard low-sugar diet but drink Ketones (BHB Salts) to clear the fog.\nStrategy B: The “Resilience Mode” (Keto Diet)Method: You restrict carbs (<20g/day) to force your liver to produce Ketones."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 11, 25844, 25900, "\nFat:EAT FAT TO SATIETY. This is your new energy source."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 24, 25900, 26046, " Do not rely on lean protein alone (chicken breast), or your body will convert the protein to sugar (Gluconeogenesis), keeping you out of ketosis."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 10, 26046, 26109, "\nTo avoid side effects, refer to the ***Keto Adaptation Guide*."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 18, 26109, 26239, "\nPart 3: THE SHIELD (Flu-Proofing & Voltage Control)\nGoal: Stabilize voltage to prevent the “Biological Crash” (Headaches/Panic).\n"], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 26239, 26241, "1."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 17, 26241, 26354, " Electrolytes (Choose Your Path)\nIf on Quick Fix, Strategy A (BHB Salts / Standard Diet):Sodium: Standard intake."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 10, 26354, 26408, " DO NOT load extra salt (Risk of High Blood Pressure)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 29, 26408, 26617, "\nPotassium:\nGoal: Install the “Brake Pads” for your nervous system.\nMechanism: Potassium Channels (KCNQ).\nThe Science: Your neurons have “brakes” called KCNQ channels that stop them from firing uncontrollably."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 6, 26617, 26653, " These brakes run on Potassium ions."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 198, 26653, 27813, " If you are low on potassium (common in high stress), your brakes fail. You can push the pedal (breathe), but the car won’t stop.\nThe Mandate: You must hit 4,700 mg of Potassium daily.\nThe Source: Food Only. (Supplements are dangerous and limited to 99mg).\nThe Menu (The “Shield” Foods):\nPotato (Baked with skin): ~925 mg (The King of Potassium).\nBeet Greens (Cooked): ~1,300 mg per cup.\nSalmon: ~1,000 mg per filet.\nAvocado: ~700-900 mg.\nCoconut Water: ~600 mg per cup.\nThe Strategy: Eat 2 large potatoes and 2 cups of greens every single day. This saturates your cells, lowering your “resting voltage” so you become physically harder to trigger.\nIf on Deep Fix, Strategy B (Keto Diet): ***See my Keto Adaptation Guide for electrolytes.***\n2. The Glutamate Shield (Anxiety):\nSulforaphane from 1 cup of broccoli sprouts (which also contain the myrosinase needed).\nFunction: It acts as a “Guardian of the Proteasome,” preventing the premature degradation of the cleanup machinery you are working so hard to build. Sulforaphane is also a potent Nrf2 activator; if you are in a “Glutamate Storm,” it helps clear oxidative stress.\nNAC: 1.8g – 2.4g (divided doses)."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 3, 27813, 27832, " Mops up glutamate."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 258, 27832, 29498, "\nAgmatine Sulfate (Optional Trial): Start with 250–500 mg in the morning or early afternoon for 3 days. If it clearly reduces the hot/itchy/reactive state without flattening mood, use 500 mg once or twice daily. For this protocol, cap at 1 g/day unless clinician-supervised.\nBest fit: Glutamate Storm + rumination/compulsion + inflammatory or neuropathic “pain-y” body state.\nPoor fit: already numb, low-drive, depressed, dissociated, low blood pressure, sedated, or entering the Dynorphin Void.\nCycle rule: use it as a 7–14 day anxiety-phase experiment, not a forever baseline. Stop if flatness, anhedonia, apathy, irritability, insomnia, dizziness, nausea, loose stools, diarrhea, or increased craving appears.\nTiming rule: avoid agmatine on D-Serine/DCS-style reconsolidation days, or keep it at least 12–24 hours away from the session.\nMagnesium Glycinate: 400mg (Night). The “Plug” for the anxiety channel.\nThe Dynorphin Bridge (Apathy / DAWS-pattern Void):Cordyceps mushrooms: A gentle vitality tool for some people, especially when the Void is mostly fatigue and low respiratory/mitochondrial drive.\nUridine Monophosphate: The more targeted option when the Void looks like dopamine-receptor burnout: low dreams, low visuals, high psychedelic tolerance, dopamine-agonist withdrawal history, or ketamine/LSD chasing. Use UMP as a 3–7 day morning trial with choline + DHA/EPA in place. Do not take it on psychedelic days.\n5-HTP: Not a dopamine tool. Use only when the parallel problem looks like low serotonin / poor sleep / TPH2 bottleneck. Do not combine with serotonergic medications, ayahuasca/harmalas, iboga, MDMA, DXM, tramadol, or same-day psychedelics.\n"], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 1, 29498, 29500, "3."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 14, 29500, 29615, " The “Nuclear Option” (Ethnobotanical)\nThe Stack: Microdose Iboga Nasal Spray (Bypasses digestion, quicker effect)."], ["Human Written", "Low", 8, 29615, 29661, " Read my iboga microdosing guide to keep safe."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 31, 29661, 29830, " While shrooms are often better for a functional mood brightener effect, iboga is its own kind of therapist that shows you what you need to see in a non-threatening way."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 6, 29830, 29872, "\nFemale Iboga: For “Numbness/Fog” (Anima)."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 20, 29872, 29997, "\nMale Iboga: For “Helplessness/Relapse” (Animus).\nShrooms: Hillbilly or Mazatapec strains are some of the best (0.1g - 0.2g)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 222, 29997, 31391, "\nPart 4: THE JAMMER (Acute Symptom Management)\nInstructions: When the symptom wave hits, identify the Type and apply the Fix.\nScenario A: The “Glutamate Storm”\nSymptoms: Anxiety, Rage, “Itchy” Brain, Racing Thoughts, Flashbacks.\nMechanism: The brain is firing too hot. You need to cool the system and jam the reconsolidation.\nThe Perry-Sequence (Rhythmic First, Visual Second)\nAnatomy overrides intellect. If your heart rate is elevated or heart-rate-variability (HRV) reduced significantly, your “Reasoning Brain” is offline.\nStep 1: Rhythmic Regulation (Brainstem): Perform 5 minutes of rhythmic, repetitive sensory input—walking, drumming on your thighs, or rhythmic “Therapeutic Sighing”.\nStep 2: Check Your Baseline: Once your heart rate is within normal range, you cerebral cortex is receptive. Phosphatidylserine (PS, see Part 2) is a daily baseline agent that lowers how often and how hard these storms hit; it’s not an in-the-moment tool.\nStep 3: Apply the Jammer: Now use Tetris or the “Color-Path Connect” game to overwrite the visual memory\nAdvanced tactic: The D-Serine Memory Re-consolidator. While L-Serine provides the building blocks for myelin, taking D-Serine (700mg–1400mg) on an empty stomach 45 minutes before a de-armoring session acts as a “memory (re)consolidator” which can cement the benefits of therapies like EMDR which aim to rewire the affective tone of memories."], ["Human Written", "High", 113, 31391, 32031, "\nD-serine has shown efficacy in studies where it was used to augment exposure therapy for treating a variety of conditions such as social anxiety, PTSD, and fear of public speaking. The idea is that it facilitates the consolidation of the newly formed memory of how the anticipated negative consequences of the exposure to what you fear didn’t actually happen. Some studies ssuggested that d-serine is more effective at this when the practice exposure to what you fear ends on a positive note as opposed to a negative one. Again, all d-serine is doing is making it easier to consolidate the memory of the experience into a long-term memory."], ["Human Written", "Low", 10, 32031, 32099, "\nUse L-Serine for daily maintenance and background hardware support."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 17, 32099, 32206, "\nUse D-Serine for acute sessions where you need to “force” memory reconsolidation. Best price from LifeLab."], ["Human Written", "High", 66, 32206, 32557, " You should take it 45 minutes or so after taking PQQ & Ketones so that your brain is fueled when the GluD dial is turned down.\nWarning: Direct D-Serine carries a higher renal (kidney) load than L-Serine. Do not exceed 30mg/kg and ensure high water intake. This risk is compounded by the higher renal load caused by a keto diet or high protein intake."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 17, 32557, 32698, "\nScenario B: The “Fog”\nSymptoms: Confusion, Disassociation, Low Energy, “Lagging.”\nMechanism: Hypometabolism (Low Fuel) or Toxicity (Static)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 94, 32698, 33237, "\nScenario C: The “Void”\nSymptoms: Numbness, Boredom, “I want to Relapse.”\nMechanism: The Dynorphin block is active. You feel “dead.” You need to force a spark. We will utilize the science of hot and cold showers as a vascular pump, and plant medicine as needed:\nFirst-Line Void Add-Ons: If the Void has a DAWS / D2-D3 burnout flavor, trial UMP before chasing more stimulation. If the Void is mainly sleep + serotonin bottleneck, trial 5-HTP at night. Do not start both together, and do not use either to force stronger psychedelic effects."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 27, 33237, 33406, "\nHot (3 Minutes): As hot as you can safely handle. This relaxes muscles and induces mild hyperthermia, signaling the body to start producing repair proteins (HSPs/PI31)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 20, 33406, 33511, "\nThe Metabolic Red Line: If your resting heart rate is elevated or HRV reduced, do NOT use high heat yet."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 52, 33511, 33808, " Heat mimics exercise and will raise your heart rate further, which can re-enforce your “armor”. Stick to lukewarm-to-cold until your baseline heart rate is below 90 BPM.\nCold (1 Minute): Turn it to max cold. This provides the acute stress spike needed to activate the transport motors (p38 MAPK)."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 5, 33808, 33833, "\nRepeat: Do this 3 times."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 4, 33833, 33853, " Always end on cold."], ["Human Written", "Low", 50, 33853, 34170, "\nFun with fungi: If the showers aren’t enough, you can microdose Hillbilly or Mazatapec (balanced, happy, spiritual) shroom strains (100-300mg daily). This stimulates 5-HT2A receptors to bypass the “numb” receptors.\nActivate the “Inner Father”: If you are lacking discipline, try a male iboga nasal spray micro-dose. "], ["Human Written", "Medium", 26, 34170, 34308, "1 spray (equal to about 150mg of bark) in the morning, as it lasts 12 hours. Make sure to check all the dangerous iboga drug interactions."], ["Human Written", "Low", 4, 34308, 34331, " Full iboga guide here."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 26, 34331, 34485, "\nPart 5: THE TIMELINE (The 8-Week Path)\nWeeks 1–2: The Glutamate Storm (Anxiety Phase)Protocol:Self-care: Hot & cold showers, alternating, ending on cold."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 12, 34485, 34558, " No hot showers if heart rate elevated or heart-rate-variability reduced."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 128, 34558, 35287, "\nSupplement daily:\nPhosphatidylserine 300–600 mg earlier in the day only if you fit the high-cortisol profile + 1 cup broccoli sprouts + Magnesium Glycinate 400 mg + NAC 1.8–2.4 g divided.\nOptional add-on: Agmatine Sulfate 250–500 mg AM, increasing to 500 mg twice daily only if it clearly reduces the hot/itchy/reactive state without flattening mood. Cap at 1 g/day in this protocol. Do not add agmatine on the same day you increase PS, start D-Serine, change NAC dose, begin keto, microdose, or introduce any other major variable.\nIf PS leaves you flat OR more wired, you’re not a high-cortisol responder — drop it. If agmatine leaves you flat, anhedonic, dizzy, nauseous, sleepless, irritable, or more craving-prone — drop it."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 11, 35287, 35350, "\nFuel: Start with BHB Salts (Strategy A) to manage initial fog."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 20, 35350, 35472, "\nRescue: “The Fire” + Chantress Seba or other music + The Repair Stack (Zn/Leu/Ser) + Tetris/Color Path for acute attacks."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 244, 35472, 36915, "\nWeeks 3–5: The Dynorphin Void (Depression Phase)State: The anxiety stops, but the world turns gray/boring.\nProtocol:Taper off Phosphatidylserine here. This phase is low-drive and gray by design — you do not want to keep blunting cortisol in an already-flattened system, or you’ll deepen the numbness. PS was for the anxiety phase; the Void phase needs the opposite. (If you never felt the wired/high-cortisol state in Weeks 1–2, you probably shouldn’t have been on PS at all.)\nAlso stop agmatine here unless it is unmistakably helping acute glutamate storms without worsening flatness. The Void phase is already low-drive and gray; agmatine can over-brake the system in the same direction.\nUMP trial if the Void looks like DAWS: 150–300 mg UMP in the morning with food for 3–7 days, with choline + DHA/EPA in place. Best fit: low dreams, weak visuals, high psychedelic tolerance, dopamine-agonist withdrawal history, ketamine/LSD craving, or dopamine-hit chasing. Do not take UMP on psychedelic days, and assume old psychedelic doses may become too strong if sensitivity returns.\n5-HTP trial if the bottleneck looks serotonergic: 50–100 mg at night for 2–3 nights, with optional P5P 10–20 mg in the morning. Best fit: poor sleep, low mood warmth, nighttime rumination, or TPH2-style serotonin synthesis bottleneck. Do not use with serotonergic medications/supplements, ayahuasca/harmalas, iboga, MDMA, DXM, tramadol, or same-day psychedelics."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 7, 36915, 36965, "\nHot & cold showers, alternating, ending on cold)."], ["Human Written", "High", 12, 36965, 37038, " No hot showers if heart rate elevated or heart-rate-variability reduced."], ["Human Written", "Low", 15, 37038, 37135, " Reduce or stop phosphatidylserine here — you don’t want to suppress an already-flattened system."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 8, 37135, 37175, " Micro-dose Male Iboga (if heart is ok)."], ["Human Written", "High", 44, 37175, 37458, "\nTransition: Consider moving to Strategy B (Keto Diet) for long-term repair (Autophagy) now that the acute storm has passed.\nRescue:\nIf Foggy: Inhale DMSO + Drink BHB.\nIf Numb: Micro-dose Male Iboga and/or Hillybilly/Mazatapec shrooms.\nWeek 8+: The BaselineState: DeltaFosB degraded."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 14, 37458, 37570, " Hardware reset complete.\nMaintenance: Cycle off NAC. Maintain metabolic flexibility (Low Carb/Seasonally Keto)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 62, 37570, 37928, "\nThe Aftermath: The Relational Vacuum\nAs the armor decays, you will experience a frightening but beautiful side effect: Interoception. Van der Kolk describes this as the ability to “feel” your own body again. For years, you have likely been numb—living in your head to avoid the pain in your chest.\nAs the dopamine armor fades, you will feel your heart beat."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 14, 37928, 37995, " You will feel your gut churn. You will feel the wind on your skin."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 7, 37995, 38040, " Do not mistake this sensitivity for anxiety."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 16, 38040, 38115, " It is not a symptom of sickness; it is the symptom of coming back to life."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 2, 38115, 38127, " Welcome it."]]}
